// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Default layout — what you get when running plain `zellij`.
//
//  Differences from zellij's built-in `default`:
//    • Uses `compact-bar` (single-line status) instead of the full status-bar +
//      tab-bar combo, and keeps it borderless. Saves a row and stays quiet.
//      Written as the alias `compact-bar`, the same spelling zellij's own
//      layouts and default.swap.kdl use (= "zellij:compact-bar").
//    • Opens TWO TABS: "main" (where you work / run nvim) and "shell".
//
//  WHY TWO TABS (the nvim-safety design):
//  Session serialization is ON (see config.kdl), so saved structure can be
//  resurrected — but Zellij may re-run a saved foreground command without its
//  original parent shell. Exiting that command can close its pane, depending
//  on the restored pane's exit handling. Closing the last pane in the last tab
//  ends the session. Keeping a separate "shell" tab means that "main" is not
//  the last tab while "shell" remains, so closing the editor pane leaves an
//  available shell. This protects the
//  session lifetime, not unsaved work or application-specific recovery.
//
//  A separate tab (rather than a split pane in the same tab) is used deliberately:
//  it gives nvim the full screen, and a whole tab is far less tempting to close by
//  reflex than an in-your-face split — so the safety net tends to stay in place.
//
//  NOTE — this is a SOFT guarantee: it holds only while the shell tab exists. If
//  you close the shell tab and then close the last editor pane, the session ends (it
//  may still be offered for resurrection if its snapshot was saved). Use
//  `zj attach --create NAME` with the actual session name. Editor session plugins
//  and backups address different recovery needs and need their own testing;
//  see docs/CONFIGURATION.md, "Session recovery, clipboard and terminal behavior".
//
//  For a single shell/tab, choose the shipped minimal layout. To edit this
//  layout directly, retain its matching default.swap.kdl; repository validation
//  requires both files. Local preferences apply only when starting through zj.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

layout {
    // Applies to every tab, including new ones (Ctrl+t then n). The `children`
    // slot is where each tab's panes go; the compact-bar sits below them.
    default_tab_template {
        children
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="compact-bar"
        }
    }

    // "main": your working tab — run nvim (or anything full-screen) here.
    tab name="main" focus=true {
        pane
    }
    // "shell": the safety-net tab — a plain shell that keeps the session alive
    // if you `:qa` out of a lone nvim in another tab. Also handy for git/commands.
    tab name="shell" {
        pane
    }
}
